versity, CNRS, IUSTI UMR 7343 and Turing Center for Living Systems, Marseille, France.\nL189: \nL190:   * PMID: 42275490\nL191:   * DOI: cite17†10.1126/science.aed5051†doi.org L192: \nL193: Item in Clipboard\nL194: # Fast cell wall softening causes Venus flytrap closure\nL195: \nL196: Jeongeun Ryu et al. Science. 2026.\nL197: \nL198: Show details\nL199: \nL200: Display options\nL201: \nL202: Display options\nL203: \nL204: Format [Select]\nL205: \nL206: [Button: Science ]\nL207: \nL208: Actions\nL209: \nL210:   * cite9†Search in PubMed L211:   * cite10†Search in NLM Catalog†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L212:   * cite3†Add to Search L213: \nL214: . 2026 Jun 11;392(6803):1183-1187.\nL215: \nL216: doi: 10.1126/science.aed5051. Epub 2026 Jun 11.\nL217: ### Authors\nL218: \nL219: cite11†Jeongeun Ryu ^{  cite18†1 }, cite13†Mathieu Colombani ^{  cite18†1 }, cite14†Corentin Mollier ^{  cite18†1 }, cite15†Joël Marthelot ^{  cite18†1 }, cite16†Yoël Forterre ^{  cite18†1 }\nL220: \nL221: ### Affiliation\nL222: \nL223:   * ^{1} Aix-Marseille University, CNRS, IUSTI UMR 7343 and Turing Center for Living Systems, Marseille, France.\nL224: \nL225:   * PMID: 42275490\nL226:   * DOI: cite17†10.1126/science.aed5051†doi.org L227: \nL228: Item in Clipboard\nL229: \nL230: [Button: Full text links ]Cite\nL231: \nL232: Display options\nL233: \nL234: Display options\nL235: \nL236: Format [Select]\nL237: \nL238: Linked Discoveries\nL239: ## Abstract\nL240: Plants can move rapidly without muscles, as seen in the Venus flytrap's snapping lobes-a long-standing puzzle in plant biomechanics. Trap closure involves an elastic instability, but the active mechanical driver has remained elusive. Using in situ hydraulic and mechanical measurements, we identified the motor driving this transition.\nL241: Closure occurs too quickly to be explained by water transport, revealing a distinct, nonhydraulic mechanism: a rapid (about one second) softening of the epidermal cell wall, releasing elastic energy stored in the trap. This represents the fastest modulation of wall mechanics reported in plants. Our finding reveals a mode of plant motility based on dynamic tuning of material properties, suggesting principles for muscle-free, bioinspired actuation.\nL242: cite19†PubMed Disclaimer L243: ## Comment in\nL244: \nL245:   * cite20†Exceeding nature's biological speed limits. L246: \nL247: Dumais J. Dumais J. Science. 2026 Jun 11;392(6803):1127-1128. doi: 10.1126/science.aei3453. Epub 2026 Jun 11. Science. 2026. PMID: 42275519\nL248: ## MeSH terms\nL249: \nL250:   * [Button: Biomechanical Phenomena ]\nL251: \nL252: Actions\nL253: \nL254:     * cite21†Search in PubMed L255:     * cite22†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L256:     * cite3†Add to Search L257: \nL258:   * [Button: Cell Wall* / physiology ]\nL259: \nL260: Actions\nL261: \nL262:     * cite23†Search in PubMed L263:     * cite24†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L264:     * cite3†Add to Search L265: \nL266:   * [Button: Droseraceae* / physiology ]\nL267: \nL268: Actions\nL269: \nL270:     * cite25†Search in PubMed L271:     * cite26†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L272:     * cite3†Add to Search L273: \nL274:   * [Button: Elasticity ]\nL275: \nL276: Actions\nL277:     * cite27†Search in PubMed L278:     * cite28†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L279:     * cite3†Add to Search L280: \nL281:   * [Button: Movement ]\nL282: \nL283: Actions\nL284: \nL285:     * cite29†Search in PubMed L286:     * cite30†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L287:     * cite3†Add to Search L288: \nL289:   * [Button: Plant Epidermis / physiology ]\nL290: \nL291: Actions\nL292: \nL293:     * cite31†Search in PubMed L294:     * cite32†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L295:     * cite3†Add to Search L296: \nL297:   * [Button: Water / metabolism ]\nL298: \nL299: Actions\nL300:     * cite33†Search in PubMed L301:     * cite34†Searc